{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the morning sun surprisingly sharp against his eyelids. He sat up in bed, a strange stiffness in his limbs. The room felt…too perfect. The wallpaper, a muted floral print he vaguely remembered hating, was flawlessly aligned. His dresser, the one he’d been meaning to replace for years, gleamed with an unnatural polish. He reached for his glasses, and as he did, a notification box popped into his vision: \"Quest: Wake Up. Reward: Basic Equipment.\" He stared, heart hammering. A notification? Basic equipment? This wasn’t his bedroom. The mundane details, the overwhelming sense of artificiality, crashed over him. He tried to open his laptop, but the screen displayed only a loading bar and the words \"Initializing System.\" Panic seized him. He was *in* something. Something digital.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of bed, navigating the overly-detailed furniture with a growing sense of dread. The hallway stretched before him, pristine and unnervingly silent. A small, pixelated health bar appeared in the corner of his vision, slowly depleting. He ran a hand through his hair, feeling the texture strangely…simulated. A cheerful chime sounded, and a quest marker appeared above the front door: \"Speak with NPC - Mrs. Higgins. Objective: Obtain Daily Tasks.\" Mrs. Higgins. Daily tasks. It was all so absurdly, undeniably, a video game. He took a shaky breath, the reality of his situation sinking in. He was trapped, a player in a world not his own, forced to follow a script he didn't write. His only hope was to figure out how to break free, but first, he had to talk to Mrs. Higgins.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.407365083694458}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00015984688070602715}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08786557614803314}, {"token": "▁morning", "logprob": -0.9802302122